hroism (Jasco J-725), 0.04 mg/mL enzyme in 10 mM Tris-HCl pH 8.0, 10 mm path length; thermal denaturation followed at 222 nm from 20 to 90 °C at 1.0 °C/min, Tm from a two-state transition fit. No CaCl2 added. Fig. 2 printed bar label 55.9 °C; Table 1 column 'Tm (°C) Ca2+ 0 mM' gives the same value for Cut190*. Split from a single flattened Tm experiment by scripts/remediation/split_tm_conditions.py (SKILL.md Step 9, ruling of 2026-08-28: a Tm measured under two conditions is two experiments).\",\"paper\":{\"id\":389,\"citation\":\"Oda, M., Yamagami, Y., Inaba, S., Oida, T., Yamamoto, M., Kitajima, S., & Kawai, F. (2018). Enzymatic hydrolysis of PET: functional roles of three Ca2+ ions bound to a cutinase-like enzyme, Cut190*, and its engineering for improved activity. Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology, 102(23), 10067-10077.\",\"title\":\"Enzymatic hydrolysis of PET: functional roles of three Ca2+ ions bound to a cutinase-like enzyme, Cut190*, and its engineering for improved activity\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s00253-018-9374-x\",\"year\":2018,\"authors\":\"Oda, M.; Yamagami, Y.; Inaba, S.; Oida, T.; Yamamoto, M.; Kitajima, S.; Kawai, F.\",\"journal\":\"Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology\",\"corresponding_author_country\":\"Japan\"},\"protein_variant\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-08-29T01:37:28.423173Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-29T19:38:36.771642Z\",\"substrate_kind\":null}],\"plastics\":[{\"id\":16,\"name\":\"PET\",\"full_name\":\"Poly(ethylene terephthalate)\",\"abbreviation\":\"PET\",\"polymer_class\":null,\"parent_id\":null,\"smiles\":null,\"cas_number\":null},{\"id\":48,\"name\":\"PBSA\",\"full_name\":\"Poly(butylene succinate-co-adipate)\",\"abbreviation\":\"PBSA\",\"polymer_class\":null,\"parent_id\":null,\"smiles\":null,\"cas_number\":null},{\"id\":47,\"name\":\"PBS\",\"full_name\":\"Poly(butylene succinate)\",\"abbreviation\":\"PBS\",\"polymer_class\":null,\"parent_id\":null,\"smiles\":null,\"cas_number\":null}],\"interactions\":[{\"id\":3800,\"plastic\":{\"id\":16,\"name\":\"PET\",\"abbreviation\":\"PET\"},\"actor_type\":\"protein_variant\",\"result\":\"positive\",\"notes\":\"The paper's central claim. Cut190 (S226P/R228S) degraded PET in bulk above 60 degC: 13.5% weight loss of amorphous PET-GF film and 27.0% of the PET-S package after 3 days at 63 degC, with TPA yields that agree with the gravimetry (10.9% and 26.2%), against zero weight loss in the enzyme-free controls. SEM showed clear erosion at 60 and 65 degC and none at 50 degC. At 50 degC the enzyme only hydrophilises the surface, as the wild type does. The authors attribute the PET-S / PET-GF difference to chain orientation (injection moulding vs extrusion) and to the 1-4% minor comonomers usual in commercial PET packaging; Table S2 shows the two films share Tg (76 degC), Tm (247 degC), Mn, Mw and Mn/Mw and differ mainly in Tc (133 vs 140 degC).\",\"strain_occurrence\":null,\"paper_id\":230,\"paper\":{\"id\":230,\"citation\":\"Kawai, F., Oda, M., Tamashiro, T., Waku, T., Tanaka, N., Yamamoto, M., Mizushima, H., Miyakawa, T., & Tanokura, M. (2014). A novel Ca2+-activated, thermostabilized polyesterase capable of hydrolyzing polyethylene terephthalate from Saccharomonospora viridis AHK190. Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology, 98(24), 10053-10064. https://doi.org/10.1007/s00253-014-5860-y\",\"title\":\"A novel Ca2+-activated, thermostabilized polyesterase capable of hy...\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s00253-014-5860-y\",\"year\":2014,\"authors\":\"Kawai, F.; Oda, M.; Tamashiro, T.; Waku, T.; Tanaka, N.; Yamamoto, M.; Mizushima, H.; Miyakawa, T.; Tanokura, M.\",\"journal\":\"Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology\",\"corresponding_author_country\":\"Japan\"},\"experiments\":[{\"id\":9815,\"method\":\"weight_loss\",\"temperature\":63,\"temperature_unit\":\"C\",\"ph\":8.2,\"buffer\":null,\"duration\":3,\"duration_unit\":\"days\",\"substrate_form\":\"amorphous_film\",\"sole_carbon_source\":null,\"culture_medium\":null,\"aerobicity\":null,\"substrate_crystallinity_pct\"