ted a 20-um agricultural mulching film within 5 h at 48 degC. Catalytic efficiency on PBSA is about 20-fold that on the small model substrate pNPB.\",\"strain_occurrence\":null,\"paper_id\":230,\"paper\":{\"id\":230,\"citation\":\"Kawai, F., Oda, M., Tamashiro, T., Waku, T., Tanaka, N., Yamamoto, M., Mizushima, H., Miyakawa, T., & Tanokura, M. (2014). A novel Ca2+-activated, thermostabilized polyesterase capable of hydrolyzing polyethylene terephthalate from Saccharomonospora viridis AHK190. Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology, 98(24), 10053-10064. https://doi.org/10.1007/s00253-014-5860-y\",\"title\":\"A novel Ca2+-activated, thermostabilized polyesterase capable of hy...\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s00253-014-5860-y\",\"year\":2014,\"authors\":\"Kawai, F.; Oda, M.; Tamashiro, T.; Waku, T.; Tanaka, N.; Yamamoto, M.; Mizushima, H.; Miyakawa, T.; Tanokura, M.\",\"journal\":\"Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology\",\"corresponding_author_country\":\"Japan\"},\"experiments\":[{\"id\":9822,\"method\":\"clear_zone\",\"temperature\":null,\"temperature_unit\":\"C\",\"ph\":null,\"buffer\":null,\"duration\":null,\"duration_unit\":null,\"substrate_form\":\"emulsion\",\"sole_carbon_source\":null,\"culture_medium\":null,\"aerobicity\":null,\"substrate_crystallinity_pct\":null,\"substrate_mw\":null,\"substrate_mw_unit\":null,\"analytical_grade\":false,\"assay_result\":null,\"assay_result_notes\":null,\"detection_limit\":null,\"detection_limit_unit\":null,\"quantitation_ceiling\":null,\"quantitation_ceiling_unit\":null,\"initial_mass\":null,\"initial_mass_unit\":null,\"observations\":[{\"time_point\":null,\"time_point_unit\":null,\"sd\":null,\"n\":null,\"control_value\":null,\"measurement_type\":\"clear_zone_diameter\",\"value\":null,\"unit\":\"mm\",\"text_description\":\"Largest clear halo of the seven polyesters on LB/0.1% polyester agar; the apparent-activity rank is PBSA > PBS, PCL > Ecoflex > PHB, PDLA > PLLA. No zone diameter is reported.\"}]},{\"id\":9823,\"method\":\"turbidity\",\"temperature\":37,\"temperature_unit\":\"C\",\"ph\":8.2,\"buffer\":null,\"duration\":30,\"duration_unit\":\"minutes\",\"substrate_form\":\"emulsion\",\"sole_carbon_source\":null,\"culture_medium\":null,\"aerobicity\":null,\"substrate_crystallinity_pct\":null,\"substrate_mw\":100000,\"substrate_mw_unit\":\"g/mol\",\"analytical_grade\":false,\"assay_result\":null,\"assay_result_notes\":null,\"detection_limit\":null,\"detection_limit_unit\":null,\"quantitation_ceiling\":null,\"quantitation_ceiling_unit\":null,\"initial_mass\":null,\"initial_mass_unit\":null,\"observations\":[{\"time_point\":null,\"time_point_unit\":null,\"sd\":null,\"n\":null,\"control_value\":null,\"measurement_type\":\"turbidity_change\",\"value\":null,\"unit\":null,\"text_description\":\"Cut190 (S226P/R228S) cleared the PBSA suspension, measured as a fall in OD600 over 30 min at 37 degC. The Ca2+ optimum for PBSA was 2.5-5.0 mM (100% activity), with more than 90% at 10-50 mM and a decline above that - unlike pNPB hydrolysis, which needed more than 300 mM Ca2+.\"},{\"time_point\":null,\"time_point_unit\":null,\"sd\":null,\"n\":null,\"control_value\":null,\"measurement_type\":\"activity_detected\",\"value\":null,\"unit\":null,\"text_description\":\"With 25-50 mM Ca2+ more than 100% of the PBSA-hydrolysing activity remained after 1 h at 60 degC relative to the unheated control - the enzyme is thermally activated rather than inactivated over this range. The PBSA degradation rate was higher at pH 8.2 than at pH 7.0, although the pNPB optimum is pH 6.5-7.0.\"}]},{\"id\":9824,\"method\":\"visual_inspection\",\"temperature\":48,\"temperature_unit\":\"C\",\"ph\":8.2,\"buffer\":null,\"duration\":5,\"duration_unit\":\"hours\",\"substrate_form\":\"film\",\"sole_carbon_source\":null,\"culture_medium\":null,\"aerobicity\":null,\"substrate_crystallinity_pct\":null,\"substrate_mw\":null,\"substrate_mw_unit\":null,\"analytical_grade\":false,\"assay_result\":null,\"assay_result_notes\":null,\"detection_limit\":n